      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "id": "cs-uge-appc-u1b-mainfn-def",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Master Atlas of the 9 Main Parent Functions & Universal Transformation Law",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Every algebraic and elementary transcendental model is built by transforming one of the <strong>nine core parent functions</strong> via \\(g(x) = a\\,f(x - h) + k\\), where \\(|a|\\) scales vertically (reflecting across the \\(x\\)-axis if \\(a < 0\\)), \\(h\\) shifts horizontally, and \\(k\\) shifts vertically:</p><table class=\"exam-table\" style=\"margin-top:6px\"><thead><tr><th>Family</th><th>Transformed Form \\(g(x)\\)</th><th>Domain</th><th>Range (\\(a > 0\\))</th><th>Key Geometric Feature</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Constant</strong></td><td>\\(f(x) = c\\)</td><td>\\((-\\infty, \\infty)\\)</td><td>\\(\\{c\\}\\)</td><td>Horizontal line, slope \\(0\\)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Linear</strong></td><td>\\(a(x - h) + k\\)</td><td>\\((-\\infty, \\infty)\\)</td><td>\\((-\\infty, \\infty)\\)</td><td>Constant slope \\(m = a\\), pivot \\((h, k)\\)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Quadratic</strong></td><td>\\(a(x - h)^2 + k\\)</td><td>\\((-\\infty, \\infty)\\)</td><td>\\([k, \\infty)\\)</td><td>Parabola vertex \\((h, k)\\), axis \\(x = h\\)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cubic</strong></td><td>\\(a(x - h)^3 + k\\)</td><td>\\((-\\infty, \\infty)\\)</td><td>\\((-\\infty, \\infty)\\)</td><td>Inflection center \\((h, k)\\), S-curve</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Absolute Value</strong></td><td>\\(a|x - h| + k\\)</td><td>\\((-\\infty, \\infty)\\)</td><td>\\([k, \\infty)\\)</td><td>V-corner vertex \\((h, k)\\), slopes \\(\\pm a\\)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Radical</strong></td><td>\\(a\\sqrt{x - h} + k\\)</td><td>\\([h, \\infty)\\)</td><td>\\([k, \\infty)\\)</td><td>Endpoint \\((h, k)\\), half-parabola</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Rational</strong></td><td>\\(\\dfrac{a}{x - h} + k\\)</td><td>\\(x \\neq h\\)</td><td>\\(y \\neq k\\)</td><td>Vertical asymptote \\(x = h\\), horizontal \\(y = k\\)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Exponential</strong></td><td>\\(a \\cdot 2^{x - h} + k\\)</td><td>\\((-\\infty, \\infty)\\)</td><td>\\((k, \\infty)\\)</td><td>Horizontal asymptote \\(y = k\\), anchor \\((h, a+k)\\)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Logarithmic</strong></td><td>\\(a\\ln(x - h) + k\\)</td><td>\\((h, \\infty)\\)</td><td>\\((-\\infty, \\infty)\\)</td><td>Vertical asymptote \\(x = h\\), anchor \\((h+1, k)\\)</td></tr></tbody></table>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
